@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Team API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Team API Permissioning functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki team with the name "Engineering Team" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Development Team |
	| Engineering Team |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Create team attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki teams should not be able to be created by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I attempt to create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"

Scenario: View team attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki teams should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team" as a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Update team attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki teams should not be able to be updated by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I attempt to update a team with the name "Development Team" to have the new name "Engineering Team" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Engineering Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Engineering Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team" as a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" as a non permissioned user

