	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I create an external link on a team "Development Team" with the following values
	| Domain      | devteam |
	| Entity Id   | 1234    |
	| Entity Name | DevTeam |
	And I attempt to delete an external link with the entity id "1234" on the team "Development Team" as a non permissioned user
	Then the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the team "Development Team" with the following values
	| Domain      | devteam |
	| Entity Id   | 1234    |
	| Entity Name | DevTeam |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" on the team "Development Team" should not be visible to a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team" using the external link domain "devteam" and entity name "DevTeam" and entity id "1234" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Set team permissions attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki team permissions should not be able to be set by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             | |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     | |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             | |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Region                | United States                            | |
	| Status                | Active                                   | |
	| Tier                  | T4                                       | |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | |
	And I create a team with the name "Development Team" for the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I attempt to set the permissions for a team with the name "Development Team" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a team with the name "Development Team" to have the new name "Engineering Team" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Engineering Team"
	And the team with the name "Development Team" should be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the team with the name "Engineering Team" should not be part of the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki team with the name "Development Team" as a non permissioned user
	And I should not be able to view an assigned account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" for the team "Development Team" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Unset team permissions attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki team permissions should not be able to be unset by non permissioned users.

	Given I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  | |
	| Contact Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken | |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     | |
